		end 'owner'
	end 'paramDefaultOwnerName'

	// ⭐ **PARSE EVERY CAPTURED DEFAULT AS ITS OWN FUNCTION** — the drain,
	// run once at the end of `parseModule`, when the last top-level declaration has closed and NO function
	// is open. That timing is the whole design: see `parseFunctionParameters`' capture site for why parsing
	// a helper in place would be `parseClosureExpression`'s ~25-alias save/restore, and why draining here
	// needs none of it. A FIELD default needs it for a second reason of its own: a `Self{}` written ABOVE
	// the field it defaults must still get that default (`field-defaults.method-before-field`), and a drain
	// at end-of-file is the only point at which declaration ORDER inside a type body cannot matter.
	//
	// It runs BEFORE `reportUnusedTypeAliases`, because a default expression can be the only USE of an alias
	// in its file (`items IntArray = [1, 2, 3]` names `IntArray` in the type, but `let n = Count.max` in a
	// default names one nothing else need mention). Reported first, that alias would be called unused on the
	// strength of code the parser had not read yet.
	//
	// ⚠ The list cannot grow while it is drained. A parameter default can only reach a parameter list
	// through a CLOSURE literal, and `captureParamDefault` refuses a default there; a field default can only
	// be captured from a `type` body, and an expression declares no type.
