		// the module is at file scope from here on — so it is closed here rather than left for whatever reads
		// the parser next to be surprised by.
		self.closeTypeParamScope()
	end 'parseDefaultHelpers'

	// The name the SWEEP published for this captured default — the mechanism's one mint, read back rather
	// than re-derived (see `captureParamDefault`). It panics rather than falling back to a fresh mint,
	// because a fallback would emit a function under a name no call site can be calling: the callers were
	// compiled against the sweep's answer, so a disagreement is a missing symbol at LINK time with no source
	// position.
	//
	// It is asked at the DRAIN and not at the capture, deliberately. The sweep is tolerant and abandons a
	// declaration it cannot read (a malformed return type, which it reads AFTER the parameter list the real
	// parse has already captured from); asked at the capture, that would panic ahead of the positioned
	// diagnostic the real parse is about to raise for the same malformed declaration. Asked here, a file
	// whose parse throws never reaches the drain at all.
	function sweptParamDefaultHelperName(ownerName ByteArray, paramIndex ParamCount) returns immutable ByteArray
		match self.signatures.defaultsOf(ownerName) 'swept'
			allRequired then break
			defaults(info) then return self.requireSweptHelperName(info.producerFor(paramIndex), ownerName: ownerName, paramIndex: paramIndex)
		end 'swept'

		return self.requireSweptHelperName(ParamDefaultProducer.required, ownerName: ownerName, paramIndex: paramIndex)
	end 'sweptParamDefaultHelperName'

	// The panic the lookup above owes when the sweep published no HELPER at the position the parse captured
	// one for — one sentence for all three ways that happens (no entry for the function at all, an entry
	// with no default at this position, or an entry calling it a CALLER-LOCATION slot), because they are one
	// defect: the two walks of one parameter list have come apart. The third way is named
	// separately in the sentence, because `callerLocationDefaultAt` is what the two would have disagreed on.
