		// read this is free — the parser meets a newline and says so, and `let x = 1 zzz` has never been
		// legal — but the helper's body is one expression lifted out of a token region, and what the
		// expression did not reach was simply abandoned: `b Integer = 7 zzz` defaulted to 7, and `b Real
		// = 1e100` defaulted to 1, because `1e100` is not a float literal (one must contain a decimal
		// point) so `e100` lexed as an identifier and vanished — a number a hundred orders of magnitude
		// wrong, silently.
		//
		// ⭐ **AND A FIELD DEFAULT INHERITS IT WHOLE**, which is why the field door built no check of
		// its own: `var v = 7 as Integer zzz` has the identical silent drop with the identical cure, and
		// `field-defaults.error.trailing-tokens` is the case that pins it here.
		//
		// ⛔ **THE STRAY TOKEN IS NAMED BY ITS TEXT, NOT BY ITS KIND.** The reader has to FIND the token
		// this refuses, and `zzz` is in the file where `identifier` is not — a message naming a spelling the
		// program does not contain would be wrong. `tokenDisplayText` is the one door that answers
		// "how does a diagnostic name this token?" (the kind's spelling only where the token carries no
		// text of its own), so this asks it rather than inlining half of it. `specs/default-values.md` —
		// the canonical definition, for the PARAMETER door — pins `'zzz'` and `'e100'`.
		try self.requireDefaultValueEnded(pending.exprEnd)
		self.finishCapabilityFacts(helper)

		// A default-value helper takes NO parameters and its return type is the parameter's own already-resolved
		// declared type (`pending.declaredType`), not a spelling this parse is standing on — so neither
		// existential column has a token to read and both stay shared-empty. A parameter declared at a
		// parameterized existential cannot have a default: `E3121`/`E2010` aside, a default is an EXPRESSION and
		// there is no literal of an interface type to write.
		self.publishExistentialInstances(helper)
