		let layoutReserve = layoutReserveFor(mayCarryALayoutDescriptor, conditionalWitnesses: 0)

		// A field default may read `countof(Self)` (`var slots = countof(Self) as Int`), so it reserves
		// the count slot on the same terms and out of the same fixpoint.
		let needsCountParam = self.signatures.anyFunctionReadsFixedElementCount() and self.signatures.functionReadsFixedElementCount(helperName)

		let helperParamCount = 1 if needsCountParam else 0

		// A synthesized helper is an ordinary declared function (see `EnclosingBodyKind`): the helpers
		// are drained at the end of the file, so a file whose last declaration is a `test` would
		// otherwise parse every default helper as though it were inside one.
		//
		// The global-alias answer is asked of the helper's own minted name, which separates the two
		// default doors. A parameter default's helper is published by the sweep
		// (`defaultHelperGlobalAliasReturn`), so `f(p T = A)` is admitted and its call site marks
		// the argument as the written-out `f(A)` is. A field default's is not, so
		// `ownedFormOfBorrowedValue` keeps the E2015 at its return. ⚠ The asymmetry is deliberate. The
		// parameter door hands the record to a call argument, where the mark is read
		// (`CapabilityCallCheck.checkCallArguments`) and a mutating callee is refused. A field
		// default hands it to a struct slot, and the mark does not survive a field store, so publishing
		// the field helper would let `var h = Holder.make(G)` followed by `h.names.push(1)` compile and
		// mutate `G`.
		//
		// A ranged-alias declared type makes the helper a ranged-return function, so the default is
		// guarded by the entry check exactly as `return <expr>` from such a function is. The brand stays
		// empty: the field door already holds the field's own.
		//
